WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.150
The great thing about the horror genre is
the range of styles it encompasses.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:09.100
Everyone's afraid of something, and some of
those unique fears have inspired amazing movies.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.890
While horror flicks often come with a sizable
body count, there's more to the genre than

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.100
just a well-stocked list of victims.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.750
From ghostly apparitions that haunt families
to the knowledge of someone stalking you,

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.359
here are the scariest horror movies where
no one actually gets offed on screen.

00:00:22.359 --> 00:00:26.159
Obviously, there are a whole bunch of spoilers
ahead!

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:27.599
Poltergeist

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:31.779
One of the most terrifying ghost story movies
of all time, Poltergeist has been parodied,

00:00:31.779 --> 00:00:36.750
referenced, and even remade, but nothing can
detract from the genuinely frightening visuals

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.480
and invasive horror of the film.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.760
"They're here!"

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.920
Luckily for the film's central family, no
one actually gets offed in Poltergeist.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:49.370
They're ultimately able to escape with their
lives intact, although they lose the safe

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.620
sanctuary that their home represented.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.900
Some would say that that's even scarier than
that truly horrific clown doll.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.900
The Others

00:00:56.900 --> 00:01:01.300
Outwardly a horror movie about a haunted house,
the real terror of The Others is in being

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.080
trapped and battered by forces you cannot
comprehend.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.030
As it turns out, the family living in fear
of ghosts are themselves the ghosts.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:11.630
What they believed to be the ghosts were,
in fact, the new owners of the house.

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:15.560
It's a twist that flips horror movie conventions
on their heads, showcasing how horrific a

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.960
ghost story can be — even for the ghost.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.880
And since the main family members were actually
ghosts the whole time, no lives are taken

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.060
in the movie itself.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.460
The Babadook

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:29.670
Like all the best horror movies, The Babadook
lets the central monster become symbolic for

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:34.889
any number of horrific real-life experiences,
like trauma, loneliness, and mental illness.

00:01:34.889 --> 00:01:38.860
The symbolic weight of the film doesn't drag
the film down into maudlin subtext, though

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:43.490
— you can enjoy it as a simple movie about
a single mother trying to keep her son safe.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.659
In spite of its frights, the characters make
it out alive in The Babadook, although viewers

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:52.130
squeamish about ill-fated family pets should
steer clear.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.740
1408

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:58.729
Based on one of Stephen King's short stories,
1408 has a simple hook that's hard to beat:

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:03.210
After the loss of his young daughter, a skeptic
rents a haunted hotel room to prove that ghosts

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.100
don't exist.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.660
"This is it?

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:08.400
You gotta be kidding me."

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:12.390
The horror in the film doesn't come from Mike's
fear of the ghosts but from his experiences

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:16.530
within a twisted reality where he can't trust
his senses or even himself.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.370
Despite the room's consistent encouragement
for him to take his own life, Mike ends up

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.989
living through the final credits.

00:02:22.989 --> 00:02:24.390
One Hour Photo

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:28.950
Robin Williams is absolutely chilling as a
voyeuristic stalker in One Hour Photo.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:32.890
The film follows Williams' character as he
becomes obsessed with a family after developing

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:33.890
their photos.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:37.720
When he discovers the family isn't as perfect
as he had believed, he begins stalking and

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.060
even threatening them.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.310
The movie works in the horror genre precisely
because of its creepy central character, the

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.120
kind of person you immediately forget about
after you leave your local store.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.530
Still, despite his creepy behavior, this obsessive
stalker doesn't actually take any lives in

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.500
the film.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.500
Signs

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.340
At one point in time, director M. Night Shyamalan
was the king of the plot twist.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:03.170
And while it might not be The Sixth Sense,
Signs is a surprisingly effective horror movie.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:06.879
The film follows a family whose grief at the
loss of their matriarch is interrupted by

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:08.220
an alien invasion.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:12.350
The horror is restrained, blending the family's
questioning faith with the arrival of alien

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:17.150
conquerors so seamlessly that some fans have
theorized that the aliens are actually demons.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:21.260
Whether the monsters are aliens or demons,
they're equally ineffective at taking any

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.450
lives in the film.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:24.950
April Fool's Day

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:28.970
The only slasher film on this list, April
Fool's Day follows a group of friends who

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:33.940
go on a weekend trip full of pranks and practical
jokes to celebrate April Fool's Day.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:38.180
Despite corpses piling up and lots of blood,
there are actually no real victims in the

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.180
film.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.950
As it turns out, each supposed victim was
actually in on the joke, helping to craft

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.709
a specialized horror resort.

00:03:44.709 --> 00:03:46.320
"Oh, ha ha.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.960
(Tidus from Final Fantasy X Impression)

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.490
That's really funny, you guys!"

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:55.609
Even a fake out finale ends up being nothing
more than a practical joke, making this the

00:03:55.609 --> 00:03:58.569
bloodiest casualty-free movie we can think
of.

00:03:58.569 --> 00:03:59.709
Thanks for watching!

